 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "nums is an integer list of length n (values may be negative or at least n). Return true exactly when nums contains every integer 0, 1, ..., n-1 exactly once, otherwise false. An empty list is a permutation of the empty range, so the answer is true. This cohort keeps its usual effects contract (the argument is never modified), so the solution works on a private copy; the preview's O(1) extra-space requirement is therefore not met and is recorded as a deviation.",
